{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1040345-pop-culture-paradigm","id":1040345,"title":"pop culture paradigm?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-29T18:34:19-08:00","id":1040345,"title":"pop culture paradigm?","content":"So.. i been reading Dune, watching the Jodorowski's documentary and thinking about a lot of pop culture and i cant stop thinking if its possible for a character to use and copy past a pop culture paradigm. like for example the whole &quot;Scott pilgrim gamer view&quot; or one more based on &quot;Dune.&quot; (a character actually believing he is a mentat). have you guys ever had to deal with something like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T18:52:31-08:00","id":1040356,"title":"","content":"I played in one game where one of the players wanted to be a pokemon trainer and our ST actually went with it.<br /> <br /> They decided that they would be specialising in Spirit magic, and their pokeballs would be Wonders designed to capture spirits too weak to escape.<br /> That would have been interesting enough on its own, but they went the extra mile and actually designed spirits, charms and all, based on the original Red/Blue Starters.<br /> <br /> If that's admissible then I'd say anything is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T19:23:22-08:00","id":1040377,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, that's how I run Orphans more often than not. They discover magic, but without anyone to guide them, what are the chances they try to use spells a la harry potter. Or jedi force powers? Left alone long enough, they refine those things into a science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T19:40:46-08:00","id":1040379,"title":"","content":"My group often enjoyed playing orphans more often than any of the standard Traditions, though I did get a bit sick at players saying, &quot;my paradigm is based off of Star Wars...&quot; <br /> <br /> Years ago I had a player who was watching the Nanoha anime and wanted her character to be a badass magical girl. That game ended up having lots and lots of explosions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T21:38:05-08:00","id":1040413,"title":"","content":"You're free to do that and it would probably happen in some corner of the Mageverse. Whether you want to feature that just depends on whether you think it's cool or not. Personally I find that kind of thing distasteful--for similar reasons that I dislike &quot;pornomancers&quot; and just about everything else in Unknown Armies. Urban fantasy walks a narrow path--too far to one side and it's full of cheesy pop culture references and disdain toward notions of mysticism and otherworldly experience. Too far to the other side, and it's just high fantasy with some cars in the way, people acting like the modern world doesn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}